      <title>Liverpool agree deal in principle with Andoni Iraola for two-year contract</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jun/02/liverpool-opened-talks-with-andoni-iraola-over-becoming-head-coach</link>
      <description>&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Negotiations with Spaniard have progressed quickly&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Assistants Tommy Elphick and Shaun Cooper to join too&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;Andoni Iraola is close to being confirmed as Liverpool’s new head coach after agreeing a deal in principle to succeed Arne Slot.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Iraola has been in talks with Liverpool’s sporting director, Richard Hughes, over replacing Slot &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/may/30/liverpool-sack-arne-slot-one-year-after-winning-premier-league-title"&gt;after the Dutchman was sacked&lt;/a&gt; on Saturday. As expected, negotiations have progressed quickly and the Spaniard is set to sign a two-year contract at Anfield.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jun/02/liverpool-opened-talks-with-andoni-iraola-over-becoming-head-coach"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
